Kars Dex security rebuild

Dex is an OpenID Connect identity provider originally developed by CoreOS,
maintained by the Dex project and its contributors:
https://github.com/dexidp/dex

This package targets Dex v2.46.1 application source at commit
75eb19238e10fc4750e7efb05a4031b254b04029 under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The unchanged upstream LICENSE is fetched from the verified source archive
and installed as /usr/share/doc/dex/DEX-LICENSE.

This is NOT the official or unmodified upstream Dex image. Kars changes the
Go toolchain, module dependency manifests and container packaging, and marks
the binary version v2.46.1-kars.1. The previous literal-OAuth-error and
historical-SAML-clock patches are obsolete with this released source and
removed. There are no Kars changes to upstream production or test files;
two added Kars regression test files retain the relevant behavior checks.
Production certificate validation, connectors, embedded web assets and real
CGO SQLite storage remain unchanged upstream implementations.

Upstream renewed the OAM fixture certificate through July 2125. The unchanged
upstream signature tests retain their real-clock default. The Kars regression
uses goxmldsig's supported fake clock to check validity within, before and
after that certificate's lifetime, without altering the certificate or XML.
The OAuth regression now targets the released server/authflow parser.
The reviewed regression sources and pinned added-file hashes
are distributed in /usr/share/doc/dex/source-patches. Complete original and
expected patched source inventories are distributed as source.upstream.sha256
and source.sha256 in /usr/share/doc/dex.

The generated dependency diff, active patched module files, and byte-for-byte
original module baselines are distributed in /usr/share/doc/dex/locks.
The four archival baselines under locks/upstream use go.mod.snapshot and
go.sum.snapshot filenames, including the api/v2 subdirectory. They are
comparison/attribution data, never compiler inputs. This path-only distinction
preserves every original byte and SHA-256 while the active patched go.mod and
go.sum retain their normal filenames and full dependency/security scanning.
Linked dependency license and notice files are distributed in
/usr/share/doc/dex/third-party.

The dependency requests match v2.46.1, including github.com/Azure/go-ntlmssp
v0.1.1 for CVE-2026-32952 and golang.org/x/crypto v0.57.0. Source preparation
selects the manifest-verified Go 1.27.2 Bookworm compiler to satisfy upstream's
Go 1.27.0 requirement, while retaining the AL3 base digest. The source preflight
still rejects unsupported requirements before resolution. Manifest inspection
is not compiler/build qualification. The checked-in generated artifact is unchanged
v2.45.1 evidence and cannot qualify this release; genuine Go generation,
reviewed promotion and full qualification are still required. The build retains the actual compiled-package
inventory as /usr/share/doc/dex/runtime-packages.json and fails if
golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp or a subpackage is linked (GO-2026-5932).
This does not suppress scanning of golang.org/x/crypto or any runtime module.

The official image's gomplate and docker-entrypoint programs are intentionally
not distributed. The supported invocation is /usr/local/bin/dex serve with an
explicit configuration file, not upstream entrypoint template expansion.

